WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.180
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.280 --> 00:01.800
There’s a party tonight.

3
00:01.840 --> 00:04.720
I want to introduce you to someone.

4
00:04.800 --> 00:06.560
You can bring your friend along.

5
00:06.560 --> 00:07.360
Don’t come.

6
00:07.360 --> 00:07.800
Why not?

7
00:08.000 --> 00:08.880
Didn’t you hear him?

8
00:08.880 --> 00:12.440
If you f*cking come, I’ll hate you for the rest of my life.

9
00:14.520 --> 00:16.720
Moth, will you paint again?

10
00:16.920 --> 00:19.400
Give me a chance to see your work again.

11
00:20.160 --> 00:21.520
I’m sorry I crossed the line.

12
00:21.920 --> 00:23.280
Is there anything I can help you with?

13
00:23.680 --> 00:24.920
Can I sleep on your lap?

14
01:59.600 --> 02:01.960
(There are times when we come up with excuses)

15
02:01.960 --> 02:05.040
(to avoid doing what we should do.)

16
02:06.040 --> 02:12.320
(But eventually, we have to find the courage to start doing it.)

17
02:26.200 --> 02:28.760
[OISHI NEKO]

18
02:35.120 --> 02:36.920
[SO I CAN JUST ASK ANYTHING?]

19
02:36.920 --> 02:38.440
[SURE.]

20
02:43.400 --> 02:46.400
[WHAT IF I’VE NEVER BEEN THE COMMITMENT TYPE,]

21
02:46.400 --> 02:48.880
[BUT ONE DAY I ASK SOMEONE TO BE WITH ME?]

22
02:48.880 --> 02:49.880
[YOU THINK IT COULD WORK?]

23
02:49.960 --> 02:52.480
[DO YOU LIKE THEM A LOT?]

24
03:01.160 --> 03:04.200
[WELL… YEAH.]

25
03:04.360 --> 03:07.520
[THEN TELL THEM. DON’T OVERTHINK IT.]

26
03:19.360 --> 03:20.440
(But sometimes…)

27
03:23.800 --> 03:25.280
(It’s harder than we thought.)

28
03:30.920 --> 03:32.079
Will you paint again?

29
03:32.800 --> 03:34.120
I am painting.

30
03:34.560 --> 03:37.840
I’m not talking about those comic characters.

31
03:50.240 --> 03:51.360
Paint again, Moth.

32
03:52.040 --> 03:54.480
Give me a chance to see your work again.

33
03:56.280 --> 03:58.640
Why don’t we try… getting together?

34
04:10.440 --> 04:11.360
What should I do?

35
04:12.520 --> 04:13.720
(About what?)

36
04:14.720 --> 04:16.680
(About art or Dean?)

37
04:17.720 --> 04:18.720
About work.

38
04:19.800 --> 04:21.320
I haven’t asked you anything about Dean yet.

39
04:21.959 --> 04:26.840
I was just telling you he asked me to be with him.

40
04:27.200 --> 04:28.320
So what are you going to do?

41
04:28.480 --> 04:29.200
Are you going to be with him?

42
04:29.520 --> 04:29.920
Pun!

43
04:31.080 --> 04:33.000
I’m asking for your advice about my painting.

44
04:33.440 --> 04:34.680
(You’re still not done with that?)

45
04:35.080 --> 04:38.280
(I told you. Just paint whatever you want.)

46
04:38.440 --> 04:40.600
(Follow your heart.)

47
04:48.360 --> 04:48.920
Well…

48
04:51.600 --> 04:53.320
I’m afraid it won’t turn out right.

49
04:53.600 --> 04:55.880
(Are you talking about the art…)

50
04:55.880 --> 04:58.640
or your relationship with Dean?

51
04:58.760 --> 05:00.200
Dean has never been the topic here.

52
05:00.440 --> 05:02.240
Hey, listen to me.

53
05:02.800 --> 05:05.880
Whatever it is, overthinking isn’t going to help.

54
05:06.480 --> 05:09.480
What you should do is give it a try.

55
05:09.600 --> 05:11.760
(Then you’ll know what works and what doesn’t.)

56
05:12.720 --> 05:16.480
(Worrying about it is only going to keep you stuck.)

57
05:19.000 --> 05:19.880
Are you free tonight?

58
05:20.600 --> 05:21.560
I need a drink.

59
05:22.720 --> 05:23.960
I have plans with Ten.

60
05:26.800 --> 05:30.400
So you’re finally getting serious with Ten, huh?

61
05:31.160 --> 05:33.200
I’ve been serious from the start.

62
05:33.880 --> 05:35.680
And I’m happy.

63
05:37.360 --> 05:39.360
Do you have a problem with that?

64
05:42.000 --> 05:42.680
No.

65
05:44.760 --> 05:46.800
Whatever it is, just tell me straight.

66
05:51.360 --> 05:57.200
If I tell you, will you promise not to get mad?

67
05:59.880 --> 06:01.680
If I got mad at you that easily, do you think

68
06:03.080 --> 06:05.520
we’d have stayed friends this long?

69
06:06.160 --> 06:06.720
(Say it.)

70
06:09.760 --> 06:18.400
Don’t you think it’s too soon to get serious with Ten?

71
06:19.800 --> 06:22.840
(In my opinion, Ten doesn’t have any flaws,)

72
06:23.440 --> 06:27.880
but you’re pretty top-tier yourself.

73
06:29.600 --> 06:31.400
If you’d waited a little longer,

74
06:32.200 --> 06:33.880
(you might’ve found yourself an even better boyfriend.)

75
06:39.640 --> 06:40.080
Okay.

76
06:41.720 --> 06:46.200
I might’ve crossed a line. I’m sorry.

77
06:48.640 --> 06:50.880
I get what you’re saying, Moth.

78
06:52.200 --> 06:53.760
But if I want to know

79
06:54.159 --> 06:56.960
whether Ten is good enough for me,

80
06:57.640 --> 06:59.440
I have to date him first.

81
06:59.680 --> 07:01.600
Then I’ll know if he’s right for me.

82
07:09.360 --> 07:14.080
Ten and I might need some time to get to know each other better.

83
07:15.400 --> 07:19.120
But right now, he makes me happy.

84
07:20.160 --> 07:22.680
Isn’t that enough?

85
07:29.880 --> 07:30.520
Yeah.

86
07:32.480 --> 07:33.640
Then go be with Ten.

87
07:34.520 --> 07:35.440
I’ll leave you alone now.

88
07:58.800 --> 08:01.800
[WHAT ARE YOU DOING?]

89
08:02.160 --> 08:05.520
[LET’S GO GRAB A DRINK.]

90
08:10.320 --> 08:11.440
[THIS GUY IS FREAKING LUCKY TO HAVE SOMEONE LIKE DR. PUN.]

91
08:11.440 --> 08:12.600
[I’LL BE HONEST. I DON’T THINK THEY’RE A GOOD MATCH.]

92
08:12.600 --> 08:13.720
[YOU SHOULDN’T MEDDLE IN OTHER PEOPLE’S BUSINESS.]

93
08:13.720 --> 08:14.920
[CARE TO ELABORATE ON “GOOD MATCH”?]

94
08:14.920 --> 08:24.920
[I’LL BE HONEST. I DON’T THINK THEY’RE A GOOD MATCH.]

95
08:25.680 --> 08:26.440
[DELETE.]

96
08:35.480 --> 08:36.440
I’m sorry.

97
08:41.880 --> 08:43.840
Why is your hair such a mess?

98
08:43.840 --> 08:47.840
Traffic was terrible, so I took a motorbike taxi.

99
08:47.960 --> 08:48.640
Gosh.

100
08:49.040 --> 08:49.880
Are you tired?

101
08:50.600 --> 08:52.960
I can come to you next time.

102
08:53.160 --> 08:53.920
That’s okay.

103
08:53.920 --> 08:55.840
It’s easier for me to come to you.

104
09:00.880 --> 09:03.880
So where are we eating today?

105
09:06.280 --> 09:08.560
I found a rooftop restaurant.

106
09:10.840 --> 09:13.120
Hey. It looks kind of romantic.

107
09:13.840 --> 09:14.640
Let’s go there.

108
09:23.200 --> 09:29.760
I got caught up with work and skipped lunch.

109
09:32.480 --> 09:33.360
Hungry.

110
09:34.080 --> 09:34.800
I believe you.

111
09:37.480 --> 09:38.720
I’m sorry, Pun.

112
09:38.960 --> 09:40.960
Instead of taking you to a fancy restaurant,

113
09:41.520 --> 09:42.960
we ended up eating noodles.

114
09:45.160 --> 09:46.160
It’s all good.

115
09:46.960 --> 09:49.080
Eating together is enough to make me happy.

116
09:50.760 --> 09:52.920
Besides, this place makes great food.

117
09:54.200 --> 09:55.440
I have it all the time.

118
10:00.440 --> 10:01.240
Hmm…

119
10:01.680 --> 10:02.280
Good?

120
10:03.400 --> 10:04.280
It’s really good.

121
10:05.000 --> 10:06.320
See? I told you.

122
10:07.160 --> 10:08.240
Or maybe you’re just hungry?

123
10:08.720 --> 10:09.320
No.

124
10:09.960 --> 10:11.880
It’s because I’m eating with you.

125
10:20.000 --> 10:21.080
I’m off tomorrow.

126
10:22.160 --> 10:24.240
Can I come cook for you at your place?

127
10:25.120 --> 10:27.200
I’ll make enough to keep in the fridge for later.

128
10:28.640 --> 10:33.640
That way, you won’t let yourself go hungry like this when you’re busy.

129
10:34.400 --> 10:35.560
I can’t tomorrow.

130
10:36.240 --> 10:37.600
There’s an award ceremony tomorrow.

131
10:38.080 --> 10:40.200
The film I edited won an award.

132
10:43.840 --> 10:47.040
Wait, you’re a film editor too?

133
10:48.120 --> 10:51.320
I thought you only edited content videos.

134
10:53.720 --> 10:58.000
Actually, editing films is my main job.

135
10:59.400 --> 11:04.720
I only edit videos for Dean to help him out.

136
11:06.520 --> 11:09.840
What’s the title of the film you edited?

137
11:11.120 --> 11:12.560
You wouldn’t know it.

138
11:12.640 --> 11:15.720
It’s an indie film. Not very well-known.

139
11:16.160 --> 11:16.960
So what?

140
11:18.480 --> 11:20.000
It’s an award-winning film.

141
11:21.360 --> 11:22.680
Well, yes.

142
11:31.520 --> 11:34.680
Why didn’t you tell me this was your job?

143
11:37.280 --> 11:42.840
I didn’t think you’d be interested in films.

144
11:43.280 --> 11:47.440
It’s pretty much the opposite of your world.

145
11:50.200 --> 11:53.720
Anything about my boyfriend, of course I’d want to know.

146
11:56.760 --> 12:01.880
Then how about we go to the event together tomorrow?

147
12:03.400 --> 12:03.880
Sure.

148
12:06.280 --> 12:07.000
Eat up.

149
12:25.040 --> 12:26.840
I haven’t even finished 10% of my painting.

150
12:29.800 --> 12:30.840
But you should eat.

151
12:31.720 --> 12:32.800
Or I’ll feed you myself.

152
12:34.720 --> 12:35.880
Feed me if you dare.

153
12:40.080 --> 12:50.560
Do you want the normal kind of feeding… or the special kind?

154
12:51.960 --> 12:53.960
I couldn’t take a special feeding even if I wanted to.

155
12:54.720 --> 12:56.280
I still have work to finish.

156
12:57.560 --> 12:59.440
Is this work really that important?

157
12:59.440 --> 12:59.960
Hm?

158
13:01.000 --> 13:04.880
If you don’t finish it, do you have to stop calling yourself an artist?

159
13:05.800 --> 13:06.840
Is it really that bad?

160
13:11.560 --> 13:12.440
I don’t know.

161
13:15.040 --> 13:16.520
But I want to make it.

162
13:19.120 --> 13:21.440
You know, when you’re stressed,

163
13:23.120 --> 13:24.680
you’re not cute at all.

164
13:27.200 --> 13:27.920
Rephrase.

165
13:27.920 --> 13:29.720
A little less cute than usual.

166
13:32.840 --> 13:33.680
Okay, let’s do this.

167
13:34.360 --> 13:35.240
Are you free tomorrow?

168
13:37.600 --> 13:38.600
How could I be?

169
13:39.240 --> 13:40.920
I just told you I haven’t finished my work yet.

170
13:41.600 --> 13:44.000
So you’re just going to sit in front of your canvas?

171
13:44.160 --> 13:46.480
How are you supposed to come up with ideas doing that?

172
13:46.760 --> 13:49.160
Let me take you out to find some inspiration.

173
13:51.760 --> 13:52.200
Yeah?

174
13:53.760 --> 13:54.360
How?

175
13:55.360 --> 13:57.320
What do you want to do?

176
13:57.920 --> 13:59.640
Diving?

177
14:00.320 --> 14:02.360
Floral design?

178
14:03.160 --> 14:04.080
Meditation?

179
14:04.080 --> 14:06.080
A vacation overseas?

180
14:06.360 --> 14:07.840
Let’s go to Europe for a week.

181
14:08.320 --> 14:11.840
We can see some great art and maybe you’ll get inspired.

182
14:12.400 --> 14:12.840
Sounds good?

183
14:16.440 --> 14:17.800
This isn’t about finding inspiration.

184
14:24.880 --> 14:26.880
Then how would you like me to help?

185
14:33.840 --> 14:35.240
Thank you for trying to help.

186
14:37.840 --> 14:39.200
But I think I need to…

187
14:42.800 --> 14:44.400
deal with this on my own.

188
14:55.000 --> 15:00.040
Can I keep my distance from you for a while?

189
15:01.000 --> 15:03.520
I need to focus on my work.

190
15:13.720 --> 15:15.280
Oh. Great.

191
15:17.520 --> 15:22.920
Then I hope you finish your work soon.

192
15:41.440 --> 15:42.360
I’ll head home.

193
15:44.320 --> 15:44.800
Huh?

194
15:57.520 --> 15:59.920
I understand that you haven’t painted in a long time,

195
15:59.920 --> 16:01.800
so you might be a little rusty.

196
16:02.400 --> 16:03.760
But trust me, Moth.

197
16:04.120 --> 16:06.320
(You’re talented.)

198
16:06.720 --> 16:09.040
(I’m sure you’ll create a great piece.)

199
16:09.440 --> 16:12.200
I want to believe you, Mes, but right now,

200
16:14.160 --> 16:16.080
everything feels like a dead end.

201
16:16.920 --> 16:22.880
I’m not trying to pressure you, but there’s an exhibition next week.

202
16:23.360 --> 16:24.680
(If you can finish the piece in time,)

203
16:25.200 --> 16:28.600
(I might be able to show it to the curator, in case they’re interested.)

204
16:29.400 --> 16:30.520
Next week?

205
16:31.120 --> 16:32.480
I don’t want you to miss this opportunity.

206
16:33.880 --> 16:36.080
Trust me. If you can do it,

207
16:36.440 --> 16:38.400
(you’ll finally be a full-fledged artist.)

208
16:38.880 --> 16:41.280
(And you won’t have to waste your time on something that isn’t right for you.)

209
16:46.400 --> 16:47.720
I’ll try.

210
16:48.560 --> 16:52.760
(I’ll leave you to it now so you can focus on your piece.)

211
16:53.920 --> 16:54.440
(Talk later.)

212
17:28.000 --> 17:36.080
[TEN, WHERE ARE YOU?]

213
17:58.600 --> 17:59.160
Pun.

214
18:03.680 --> 18:04.680
Why are you looking at me like that?

215
18:06.080 --> 18:08.240
Am I overdressed?

216
18:08.720 --> 18:09.480
No.

217
18:11.200 --> 18:12.200
You look very handsome.

218
18:28.120 --> 18:29.960
Yay!

219
18:30.080 --> 18:31.800
One more.

220
18:32.120 --> 18:34.680
Yeah!

221
18:36.640 --> 18:37.600
Thank you.

222
18:45.200 --> 18:49.080
How come you never told me your job was such a big deal?

223
18:49.720 --> 18:52.040
Come on. That’s an overstatement.

224
18:52.640 --> 18:54.440
It’s just the indie film scene.

225
18:55.000 --> 18:58.200
Besides, I didn’t think you’d be interested in something like this.

226
18:58.560 --> 18:59.640
Of course I’m interested.

227
19:01.600 --> 19:05.400
All this time, you’re always the one bragging about me.

228
19:06.160 --> 19:12.800
But I can’t brag about you when I want to because you never tell me anything.

229
19:23.120 --> 19:31.280
Someone even said before that your profile didn’t match mine.

230
19:35.000 --> 19:36.240
But I didn’t care.

231
19:37.680 --> 19:42.120
As long as you’re sweet and kind.

232
19:48.280 --> 19:52.160
Gosh, are you just trying to comfort me?

233
19:52.400 --> 19:54.520
No. I’m serious.

234
19:56.600 --> 19:59.280
Come to think of it, maybe I’m the one

235
20:02.640 --> 20:04.640
who bagged a top-tier guy.

236
20:05.520 --> 20:06.600
You’re exaggerating.

237
20:07.120 --> 20:08.520
Not even close.

238
20:10.120 --> 20:15.880
My boyfriend is super hot and super talented.

239
20:20.640 --> 20:21.640
Let’s take a photo.

240
20:27.280 --> 20:28.040
This too.

241
20:36.280 --> 20:36.920
See?

242
20:37.360 --> 20:38.040
Hey!

243
20:38.680 --> 20:39.560
Posted.

244
20:40.760 --> 20:41.840
You really have to post that?

245
20:43.520 --> 20:44.560
Can you do that for me too?

246
20:45.360 --> 20:46.960
I’m shy.

247
20:51.600 --> 20:53.280
Mr. Dean, we’d really like to know

248
20:53.400 --> 20:54.520
why you’re not here, sir.

249
20:54.520 --> 20:56.360
We’re so sad.

250
20:56.360 --> 20:56.720
True.

251
20:56.720 --> 21:05.160
[WHAT ARE YOU DOING?]

252
21:05.160 --> 21:12.240
[MOM]

253
21:16.560 --> 21:17.240
Yes, Mom?

254
21:17.600 --> 21:20.400
(Nothing, son. I just missed you, so I called.)

255
21:23.560 --> 21:25.640
What are you doing?

256
21:25.920 --> 21:28.640
(I just finished eating. What about you?)

257
21:28.640 --> 21:29.960
(Are you going out?)

258
21:31.240 --> 21:31.880
No, Mom.

259
21:32.040 --> 21:32.640
I’ve been bored lately.

260
21:32.640 --> 21:33.400
Don’t really feel like going out.

261
21:33.880 --> 21:35.800
(Are you with Moth?)

262
21:41.320 --> 21:41.880
No.

263
21:42.120 --> 21:44.320
(Is work so busy now?)

264
21:44.360 --> 21:46.240
(Can you find some time to come home?)

265
21:46.440 --> 21:48.920
(It’s almost your dad’s birthday.)

266
21:48.960 --> 21:51.240
(Can you come home so we can celebrate together?)

267
21:51.680 --> 21:52.920
Why are we celebrating?

268
21:53.760 --> 21:55.040
We don’t usually celebrate it.

269
21:55.400 --> 21:56.440
(I don’t know.)

270
21:56.800 --> 22:00.040
(I just want to do something special for him this year.)

271
22:00.040 --> 22:03.160
(And I want you here too, so the whole family can be together.)

272
22:03.600 --> 22:04.760
(Please come home, dear.)

273
22:25.120 --> 22:26.160
Hey, Dean!

274
22:29.520 --> 22:31.080
Why didn’t you come in the morning?

275
22:31.160 --> 22:32.440
Why did you come now?

276
22:32.760 --> 22:34.960
Driving at night is dangerous.

277
22:35.360 --> 22:36.560
To avoid traffic.

278
22:37.720 --> 22:39.840
Didn’t Moth come with you?

279
22:40.240 --> 22:41.400
No, Mom.

280
22:41.840 --> 22:42.680
He’s busy.

281
22:44.200 --> 22:46.160
You didn’t ask him to come, did you?

282
22:47.880 --> 22:50.760
Even if I did, he wouldn’t be able to.

283
22:51.040 --> 22:52.400
He’s busy with important work.

284
22:52.520 --> 22:54.000
How important could it be?

285
22:54.400 --> 22:55.960
Why didn’t you ask him first?

286
22:56.120 --> 22:58.280
Maybe he wanted to come with you.

287
23:03.640 --> 23:05.360
Honey. Honey.

288
23:05.720 --> 23:06.720
Look.

289
23:07.480 --> 23:10.960
Dean rushed home to celebrate your birthday.

290
23:11.080 --> 23:13.240
He must’ve missed you so much.

291
23:16.640 --> 23:17.000
Mm.

292
23:19.160 --> 23:21.480
I’m going upstairs to hit the sack.

293
23:21.680 --> 23:22.880
Sure. Get some rest.

294
23:23.080 --> 23:25.080
Come down for breakfast tomorrow.

295
23:25.280 --> 23:26.080
Yes, Mom.

296
23:57.640 --> 24:08.560
[I’LL BE AT MY PARENTS’ HOUSE.]

297
24:08.720 --> 24:16.400
[FOR HOW LONG? WHEN WILL YOU BE BACK?]

298
24:21.360 --> 24:25.040
[DRIVE SAFE.]

299
24:32.600 --> 24:42.240
[ALREADY HERE.]

300
24:42.240 --> 25:02.600
[CAN I CALL?]

301
25:02.640 --> 25:13.760
[LET’S NOT FOR NOW.]

302
25:58.400 --> 26:01.920
[GOOD NIGHT.] [HOW ARE YOU?]

303
26:12.200 --> 26:15.760
[GO DOWNSTAIRS AND GET YOUR DELIVERY.]

304
26:19.520 --> 26:22.520
[DON’T PAINT TILL YOU FAINT. — DEAN]

305
26:26.400 --> 26:27.360
Here you go.

306
26:31.040 --> 26:34.480
[I’M STILL ALIVE.]

307
26:43.120 --> 26:45.160
[HAVE YOU FINISHED? — DEAN]

308
26:49.920 --> 26:52.200
[YOUR MUSCLES WILL GET STIFF FROM SITTING TOO LONG. — DEAN]

309
26:55.080 --> 26:57.800
[WHEN YOU SELL YOUR PAINTING, PAY ME BACK FOR THE FOOD. — DEAN]

310
27:27.840 --> 27:38.200
[I MISS YOU.]

311
27:38.240 --> 27:43.240
[MISS YOU TOO.]

312
27:57.080 --> 27:58.520
I think this is good, Moth.

313
27:59.160 --> 28:02.280
Your technique has become a lot more refined.

314
28:07.560 --> 28:09.000
You looked at it for so long.

315
28:09.800 --> 28:10.800
Is that all you’re going to say?

316
28:13.760 --> 28:15.400
Feel free to give me honest criticism.

317
28:16.280 --> 28:17.200
I can take it.

318
28:18.400 --> 28:19.440
Don’t overthink it.

319
28:21.440 --> 28:23.200
I don’t think it has any flaws.

320
28:24.880 --> 28:26.160
It’s just…

321
28:29.000 --> 28:31.120
I’ve never seen you paint anything like this before.

322
28:32.960 --> 28:34.480
You’re much more romantic now.

323
28:41.920 --> 28:46.680
But I’m really glad you’re taking painting seriously again.

324
28:53.120 --> 28:54.520
Trust me, Moth.

325
28:56.320 --> 29:01.600
This piece is going to take you somewhere.

326
29:05.280 --> 29:06.640
It’s just one painting.

327
29:08.360 --> 29:11.080
It can’t be that life-changing.

328
29:15.520 --> 29:19.960
Just getting back to doing what you should be doing is already changing your life.

329
29:30.880 --> 29:36.160
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

330
29:36.240 --> 29:37.320
I’m gonna blow it out now.

331
29:39.440 --> 29:41.920
Yeah!

332
29:41.960 --> 29:43.840
Happy birthday, Dad.

333
29:43.880 --> 29:46.360
I wish you good health and a long life.

334
29:46.360 --> 29:48.560
Live to be a hundred.

335
29:48.560 --> 29:50.520
Who actually makes it to a hundred?

336
29:52.080 --> 29:53.000
Hey, Dean.

337
29:53.280 --> 29:54.280
What’s the hurry?

338
29:54.400 --> 29:55.920
Give Dad your birthday wish first.

339
29:56.080 --> 29:58.120
He’s been getting birthday wishes since this morning.

340
29:58.280 --> 30:00.960
But the monks already blessed him this morning.

341
30:01.000 --> 30:02.280
It’s different.

342
30:02.720 --> 30:05.280
Wishes from family are the best.

343
30:09.040 --> 30:13.880
Well then, I wish Mom and Dad would always love each other like you did on day one.

344
30:14.240 --> 30:14.920
Good?

345
30:17.320 --> 30:20.160
Or… I wish you guys would look younger every day.

346
30:23.280 --> 30:25.320
Happy birthday, honey.

347
30:29.920 --> 30:31.520
Where should we cut it?

348
30:31.520 --> 30:34.560
- How do we cut the cake? - What do you think?

349
30:34.560 --> 30:35.480
I think right there.

350
30:35.480 --> 30:38.000
Here? But I think right here is better.

351
30:39.000 --> 30:40.360
Have you finished painting?

352
30:41.720 --> 30:42.800
Congratulations.

353
30:43.680 --> 30:46.560
Now you can get back to living a normal life.

354
30:46.800 --> 30:49.000
Whoa. “Living”?

355
30:50.120 --> 30:51.000
Isn’t that a bit much?

356
30:51.440 --> 30:54.440
Well, you don’t have to be cooped up in your room all day anymore.

357
30:55.320 --> 30:56.960
You can go see a movie, listen to music,

358
30:57.120 --> 30:58.280
(and eat good food.)

359
30:58.400 --> 30:59.800
(Isn’t that what living is?)

360
31:00.920 --> 31:04.720
That’s your way of living, not mine.

361
31:06.800 --> 31:08.000
(Are you still in Ratchaburi?)

362
31:08.840 --> 31:09.280
Mm.

363
31:10.240 --> 31:11.360
You’re staying quite long.

364
31:11.880 --> 31:13.360
Didn’t you say you didn’t like staying home?

365
31:14.040 --> 31:18.040
Mom wanted me to stay until Dad’s birthday.

366
31:19.280 --> 31:23.600
She wanted all her children home for his birthday for once.

367
31:25.680 --> 31:26.840
I didn’t want to say no to her.

368
31:26.960 --> 31:28.160
Dad just blew out the candle.

369
31:28.880 --> 31:29.760
That’s good.

370
31:31.880 --> 31:33.440
You’ve partied with everyone in the world.

371
31:34.040 --> 31:35.440
It’s time to party with your family for a change.

372
31:43.560 --> 31:45.040
You didn’t get into a fight with your dad, did you?

373
31:46.360 --> 31:47.080
No.

374
31:48.840 --> 31:49.960
Why would you ask that?

375
31:50.440 --> 31:52.120
Just asking.

376
31:53.320 --> 31:53.960
I don’t know.

377
31:55.680 --> 31:59.360
You told me you and your dad didn’t see eye to eye.

378
31:59.840 --> 32:03.040
We haven’t talked much, so we haven’t had a chance to fight yet.

379
32:06.400 --> 32:08.520
We’re both giving each other the silent treatment.

380
32:09.400 --> 32:10.880
Probably for the best.

381
32:16.680 --> 32:17.560
Um…

382
32:27.280 --> 32:28.280
When are you coming back?

383
32:28.720 --> 32:29.160
Aw.

384
32:30.360 --> 32:30.880
Why?

385
32:31.240 --> 32:32.760
You’re answering a question with a question now?

386
32:32.960 --> 32:35.760
You should know what I want to hear.

387
32:36.960 --> 32:39.520
Come on. Say it loud and clear.

388
32:41.720 --> 32:42.800
I miss you.

389
32:44.760 --> 32:46.200
The signal isn’t very good.

390
32:46.560 --> 32:47.840
Can you say that again?

391
32:48.160 --> 32:48.960
Enough.

392
32:51.160 --> 32:52.240
I miss you too.

393
32:54.920 --> 32:56.080
I miss you so damn much.

394
32:56.680 --> 33:00.960
I miss you so, so, so, so much more.

395
33:01.440 --> 33:02.720
Why are we competing?

396
33:03.000 --> 33:04.000
I’m not competing.

397
33:04.600 --> 33:06.840
Because if I were, I’d definitely win.

398
33:07.960 --> 33:12.080
I miss you “sooooooo” much, with a million o’s.

399
33:12.160 --> 33:13.160
I don’t believe you.

400
33:13.280 --> 33:14.800
Say that again. My heart needs some pampering.

401
33:15.000 --> 33:16.640
You’re just imagining things.

402
33:17.200 --> 33:19.360
Are you a good boy now, going to bed so early?

403
33:28.160 --> 33:29.880
Here. Keep this in your fridge.

404
33:31.520 --> 33:32.240
Thank you.

405
33:32.360 --> 33:35.040
Next time, don’t forget to bring Moth too.

406
33:35.600 --> 33:38.040
That way, you won’t be lonely when you’re home.

407
33:38.120 --> 33:39.960
Come on, Mom. I wasn’t lonely at all.

408
33:40.000 --> 33:42.200
Yes, you were.

409
33:43.960 --> 33:46.360
You’re a grown-up now.

410
33:46.560 --> 33:52.280
We all need someone by our side to be happy. Got it?

411
33:54.240 --> 33:56.520
But if you’re going to bring someone home,

412
33:56.520 --> 33:59.120
make sure you’re clear about your relationship status first.

413
33:59.320 --> 34:01.920
If you’re going to keep this up, don’t bother bringing anyone home.

414
34:02.200 --> 34:03.320
I feel bad for Moth.

415
34:04.160 --> 34:05.360
Duen!

416
34:05.560 --> 34:07.480
You’re such a buzzkill for your little brother.

417
34:08.520 --> 34:10.199
You always have to pick a fight.

418
34:10.440 --> 34:12.000
I’m just telling the truth.

419
34:13.400 --> 34:14.920
Get home safe, though.

420
34:17.360 --> 34:22.639
Thanks so much for coming home for Dad’s birthday.

421
34:31.080 --> 34:31.600
I’m taking off now, Mom.

422
34:31.600 --> 34:32.199
Okay.

423
34:32.600 --> 34:33.199
I’ll see you later.

424
34:33.880 --> 34:34.480
Bye.

425
36:26.760 --> 36:28.280
Ahem.

426
36:39.200 --> 36:40.680
Your painting is very beautiful.

427
36:43.480 --> 36:44.440
It’s freaking stunning.

428
36:50.800 --> 36:52.240
Do you really like it, or are you just trying to flatter me?

429
36:52.880 --> 36:56.120
Well, I’m not as artistic as everyone here,

430
36:58.120 --> 36:59.480
but I’m not blind.

431
37:01.960 --> 37:03.280
I can see how much

432
37:05.200 --> 37:06.520
dedication and attention

433
37:09.040 --> 37:13.320
you put into every part of the painting.

434
37:20.200 --> 37:23.880
That alone is enough to make me see how beautiful it is.

435
37:27.120 --> 37:28.760
Who said it was just dedication?

436
37:32.120 --> 37:33.880
I put my longing into it too.

437
37:45.960 --> 37:47.280
I missed you so damn much.

438
38:12.520 --> 38:13.840
Congratulations.

439
38:15.280 --> 38:16.600
Hey, Mes.

440
38:18.800 --> 38:24.240
Was it a hassle pulling strings to get my work into the showcase at the last minute?

441
38:24.880 --> 38:25.960
Who told you that?

442
38:26.360 --> 38:27.720
I didn’t pull any strings.

443
38:27.880 --> 38:31.000
I just sent your painting to the curator, and they were simply interested.

444
38:32.320 --> 38:35.840
But if you don’t believe me, look at this.

445
38:41.800 --> 38:43.920
Someone’s already interested in buying your painting.

446
38:48.840 --> 38:50.040
Are you the one buying it?

447
38:51.720 --> 38:54.080
If you are, I’m not selling.

448
38:55.080 --> 38:56.400
I’m not.

449
38:57.040 --> 38:59.240
Other people are interested in your art too.

450
39:03.000 --> 39:03.920
What about you, Dean?

451
39:04.760 --> 39:06.840
Are you interested in any of the paintings?

452
39:07.360 --> 39:08.280
I can give you some recommendations.

453
39:10.040 --> 39:10.480
Sure.

454
39:11.240 --> 39:12.480
But let me look around first.

455
39:12.640 --> 39:14.640
I’m not sure which one I want to buy.

456
39:17.200 --> 39:18.200
I’m going to use the bathroom.

457
39:24.600 --> 39:25.400
Congratulations.

458
39:26.480 --> 39:27.360
Thank you.

459
39:37.440 --> 39:37.800
Hey.

460
39:38.520 --> 39:40.080
Are you really buying that piece?

461
39:40.280 --> 39:41.960
You mean the “Beautiful Chaos” one?

462
39:43.120 --> 39:44.720
It’s pretty cheap.

463
39:44.840 --> 39:45.920
I’ll just buy it first.

464
39:46.040 --> 39:46.800
Maybe I’ll get lucky.

465
39:46.920 --> 39:48.680
The artist becomes famous someday.

466
39:49.200 --> 39:51.160
Though I seriously doubt it.

467
39:51.440 --> 39:52.880
It’ll just be another piece collecting dust in my collection.

468
39:54.680 --> 39:55.480
That’s true.

469
39:55.600 --> 39:57.440
Come on. There are plenty of other paintings to look at.

470
39:57.440 --> 39:58.320
Let’s go.

471
40:04.480 --> 40:05.280
Oh, hey.

472
40:05.720 --> 40:08.000
When are you planning to paint your next one?

473
40:08.720 --> 40:10.480
I can contact the sponsor beforehand.

474
40:11.280 --> 40:15.320
You know what? Someone wants to buy a whole collection of your work.

475
40:15.760 --> 40:17.080
We could strike a deal early.

476
40:18.800 --> 40:19.920
I don’t know yet.

477
40:21.000 --> 40:23.720
I have to finish up my ongoing work for my clients first.

478
40:24.640 --> 40:26.920
I still have a lot of projects pending.

479
40:27.840 --> 40:29.360
And I don’t want to push the deadlines back any further.

480
40:31.720 --> 40:34.000
I want you to take your future more seriously.

481
40:41.040 --> 40:42.640
I am taking it seriously.

482
40:43.360 --> 40:48.080
I mean, you should think about what truly matters in your life,

483
40:50.000 --> 40:54.040
not something that distracts you from the path you should be on.

484
40:57.160 --> 40:58.880
How much is this piece? I’m buying it.

485
40:59.200 --> 41:00.160
How much did you sell it for?

486
41:00.360 --> 41:01.320
I’ll pay double.

487
41:02.560 --> 41:03.360
What’s gotten into you?

488
41:03.600 --> 41:06.600
Because I know how hard you worked on this piece.

489
41:08.160 --> 41:10.320
This work deserves to be more than just

490
41:10.320 --> 41:12.200
another meaningless piece in someone’s collection.

491
41:13.720 --> 41:17.880
The guy buying it doesn’t even know how much work you put into it

492
41:17.880 --> 41:21.640
or how many all-nighters you pulled to finish it.

493
41:21.720 --> 41:24.320
It’s already reserved.

494
41:24.440 --> 41:25.600
Do you have the buyer’s number?

495
41:27.760 --> 41:28.720
I still want it.

496
41:31.080 --> 41:32.040
It’s okay.

497
41:38.680 --> 41:39.680
It really is okay.

498
41:41.200 --> 41:42.240
It’s just a painting.

499
41:43.800 --> 41:45.280
It’s not that valuable.

500
41:46.800 --> 41:47.720
Let’s just sell it.

501
41:51.000 --> 41:51.280
But—

502
41:51.280 --> 41:52.200
Go wait for me outside.

503
42:10.120 --> 42:11.400
Thank you so much, Mes,

504
42:13.280 --> 42:18.640
for pushing me and believing in me all this time.

505
42:21.840 --> 42:25.480
But I can’t be the same person who believed

506
42:26.520 --> 42:30.880
and painted because of you anymore.

507
42:33.880 --> 42:35.600
Because I’ve realized that

508
42:37.600 --> 42:42.320
I should dedicate myself to what truly matters in my life.

509
42:44.440 --> 42:45.720
What do you mean, Moth?

510
42:47.520 --> 42:51.360
Your opportunity and your worth are right here.

511
42:54.440 --> 42:56.920
(How would you like me to help?)

512
42:58.000 --> 42:58.960
(I miss you.)

513
42:59.440 --> 43:00.520
(I miss you too.)

514
43:01.160 --> 43:02.600
(I missed you so damn much.)

515
43:05.320 --> 43:09.560
I think we should go our separate ways, Mes.

516
43:15.880 --> 43:16.920
Will you excuse me?

517
43:30.760 --> 43:31.360
Where are we going?

518
43:31.840 --> 43:32.720
You done with the exhibition?

519
44:13.720 --> 44:15.320
Save your money for something else.

520
44:16.680 --> 44:18.040
Why would you buy my painting?

521
44:19.000 --> 44:20.480
Wouldn’t it be nice if I owned it?

522
44:22.880 --> 44:28.920
Well, it’s not like it’ll be the last painting I ever make.

523
44:31.000 --> 44:32.560
I can always paint another one when I’m in the mood.

524
44:33.880 --> 44:35.160
You can buy it then.

525
44:57.080 --> 44:58.440
Can I stay over at your place tonight?

526
45:01.320 --> 45:02.520
Let’s make something to eat.

527
45:08.520 --> 45:10.280
Will you stop being so cute?

528
45:12.160 --> 45:15.840
If I were so crazy about you that I lost my mind, what would I do?

529
45:54.240 --> 45:54.880
Making rice porridge?

530
45:55.080 --> 45:55.400
Yeah.

531
45:58.960 --> 45:59.840
You smell good.

532
46:00.320 --> 46:01.120
Duen’s calling.

533
46:01.320 --> 46:01.720
Why are you calling—

534
46:01.720 --> 46:04.000
Dad was admitted to the hospital last night. He needed emergency surgery.

535
46:04.080 --> 46:05.320
Dean, you should come home.

536
46:05.480 --> 46:06.840
If I go, how can I help him?

537
46:06.840 --> 46:08.920
Or will I just make him feel worse?

538
46:09.320 --> 46:11.920
Just having you there is good enough.

539
46:12.240 --> 46:13.640
Do you want me there with you?

540
46:13.880 --> 46:16.880
Please take care of my little brother, Moth.
